          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"fore, we could not claim the merit of saints, though we did not\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"enjoy pleasures \u0938\u094b\u0922\u093e\u0903\u2014We had to put up with the inclemencies\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"of the weather &c. on account of poverty (as R\u00e2marshi suggests)\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"but that does not entitle us to the merit of penance. \u0927\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0924\u0902\u2014We\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"were engaged in contemplation, not of the feet of S'iva but of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"wealth Thus though we did the same actions that are done by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"sages, viz forgiving, renunciation, endurance, and contemplation,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"as to the fruits of those actions we have been deceived. We\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"went the wrong way, and hence our disappointment. For \u0928\u093f\u092f-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"\u092e\u093f\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0923\u0947\u0928 \u0936\u092e\u094d\u092d\u094b\u0903 \u092a\u0926\u0902 cf \u0905\u0928\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0948\u0936\u094d\u091a \u0938\u0941\u0938\u0942\u0915\u094d\u0937\u094d\u092e\u0948\u0930\u094d\u0928\u093f\u092f\u092e\u093f\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0923\u093e\u0926\u093f\u092d\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0943\u0917\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947 Vik,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"I. 1 The fig is \u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937\u094b\u0915\u094d\u0924\u093f.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit in lines 9\u201310 is difficult to read.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 8. \u0935\u092f\u092e\u0947\u0935 \u092d\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924\u093e\u0903\u2014desire ( which was never satisfied ) has\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"preyed on our minds ( like canker on a bud ). Some supply\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0915\u093e\u0932\u0947\u0928 but that idea is expressed in \u092f\u093e\u0924\u093e\u0903. \u0924\u092a\u094d\u0924\u093e\u0903\u2014i. e. with cares\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"and anxieties. \u0935\u092f\u092e\u0947\u0935 \u092f\u093e\u0924\u093e\u0903-our bodies have been wasted away; or\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"it is we (men) that have had our exits. In popular language we\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"say that time passes; but really speaking it is not time that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"passes: time is eternal; but we have our exits from this world.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"\u0924\u0943\u0937\u094d\u0923\u093e \u0928 \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u0923\u093e\u2014cf next sl. \u00b0\u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u0923\u093e weakened by old age.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl 9 All parts of the body indicate the advent of old age.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"Greed alone grows young, i. e., though old we feel as greedy as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"when we were young, or even more. \u0906\u0915\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0902-Over-ridden; on\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"which a footing has been made by \u092a\u0932\u093f\u0924\u0902\u2014gray hair: \u092a\u0932\u093f\u0924\u0902 \u091c\u0930\u0938\u093e\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0936\u094c\u0915\u094d\u0932\u094d\u092f\u0902 Amara. \u0924\u0943\u0937\u094d\u0923\u093e here may also be taken as an \u0909\u092a\u0932\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0923 i. e.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"indicating kindred things\u2014the feelings of the mind. \u0924\u0930\u0941\u0923\u093e\u092f\u0924\u0947\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0924\u0930\u0941\u0923\u0940 \u0907\u0935\u093e\u091a\u0930\u0924\u093f is young Cf. \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0947 \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0903 \u0915\u0947\u0936\u093e \u0926\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093e \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093f \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0903 \u0964\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0936\u094d\u091a\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0941\u0937\u0940 \u0936\u094d\u0930\u094b\u0924\u094d\u0930\u0947 \u0924\u0943\u0937\u094d\u0923\u0948\u0915\u093e \u0924\u0930\u0941\u0923\u093e\u092f\u0924\u0947 Pt. V. 16.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit quotation and dictionary reference are somewhat unclear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 10. \u092a\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0937\u092c\u0939\u0941\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0903\u2014R\u00e2marshi explains this as equivalent\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"to \u092a\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0937\u0938\u092e\u094d\u092c\u0928\u094d\u0927\u0940 \u092a\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0937\u093e\u0923\u093e\u0902 \u092f\u0942\u0928\u093e\u0902 \u092f\u094b \u092d\u0935\u0924\u0940\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0903, which is equivalent to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u092a\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0937\u0924\u094d\u0935\u0935\u093f\u0937\u092f\u0915\u0903: another way is to take it as \u092a\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0937\u0947\u0937\u0941 \u092c\u0939\u0941\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0903 respect\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"among men. The first is preferable. \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928\u093e\u0903-of equal age or rank;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"contemporary. \u091c\u0940\u0935\u093f\u0924\u0938\u092e\u093e\u0903\u2014equal to life, valued or esteemed\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"as life itself. The other interpretation placed on this viz.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u091c\u0940\u0935\u093f\u0924\u0902 \u0938\u092e\u0902 \u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923\u0902 \u092f\u0947\u0937\u093e\u0902 can hardly be acceptable. \u0938\u094d\u0935\u0930\u094d-The word is an\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit in lines 2\u20133 is difficult to distinguish.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 53 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"7\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"8\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"9\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"10\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r5\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
